# API Module Structure

## Layout

One domain folder under `api/src/modules/<domain>/` with:

- `domain.module.ts`
- `domain.controller.ts`
- `domain.service.ts`
- `domain.entity.ts`
- `domain.dto.ts` (as needed)

Register each module in `app.module.ts`. Export the service if other modules depend on it.

## Controllers

- Keep controllers thin: route + guard + delegate to service.
- Use singular route prefix: `@Controller('level')`.
- Protect routes with `SessionGuard` + `@CurrentSession()`.

```ts
@Controller('level')
export class LevelController {
  @UseGuards(SessionGuard)
  @Get()
  getAll(@CurrentSession() session: Session) {
    return this.levelService.getAllFromUser(session.userId);
  }
}
```

## Global modules

Use `@Global()` sparingly for cross-cutting concerns (`SessionModule`, `MailerModule`, `AppConfigModule`).
